{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["The reason for <b>your brother</b> — that he warns him because he is your brother, even though you are not included in 'Aaron your brother shall not come.' Ibn Ezra said (on Leviticus 16:1) that this pericope serves as a sign that the sons of Aaron brought the fire of the incense inside. But in my opinion this is not so, for the verse that mentions the sin always says (Numbers 3:4), 'when they offered strange fire.' And if there would be proof that they entered inside because of the warning that He gave to Moses concerning their father, lest he die — all the more so would there be proof that they entered drunk on wine, because of the warning that was said to Aaron himself immediately afterward. Furthermore, how could it enter their minds to come on that day to a place where their father had never entered, for Aaron burned the incense on the inner altar — why would they bring their incense further inside than his? I have already hinted (Ramban on Leviticus 10:2) at their sin, and the language of the verses points to it. But the phrase 'as they approached' according to the plain sense, like 'or as they approached the altar to minister' (Exodus 30:20; 40:32), means that while they ministered before YHWH they died. If so, He warns Aaron that he should minister only in the place that he is commanded and at the time that he is commanded. And it is possible that the reason is as our Sages said (Mekhilta Beshallah VaYissa 6), that they were criticizing after the incense, through which Nadab and Abihu died, etc. And the verse says: After the death of the two sons of Aaron, as they approached before YHWH with the incense, YHWH said to Aaron — for he would draw nearer to YHWH than they with the incense, and he would die if he entered the Sanctuary without the incense, for with it he must enter first, as He said: 'And he shall bring it inside the veil' (Leviticus 16:12), 'and the cloud of the incense shall cover the mercy-seat that is over the Testimony, and he shall not die' (Leviticus 16:13). And this is the reason for 'for in the cloud I will appear upon the mercy-seat' — that he should enter only with the incense whose cloud rises there, as He said (Leviticus 16:12–13), 'and the cloud of the incense shall cover the mercy-seat.'" "The reason for <b>at all times</b> — since He has already mentioned the Day of Atonement, for He said (Exodus 30:10), 'And Aaron shall make atonement on its horns once a year,' He says here: he shall not come into the Sanctuary at any time except with this, that is, on the day that he offers these sacrifices for atonement. Afterward He specifies in the pericope how he shall enter, as He said (Leviticus 16:12), 'And he shall bring it inside the veil,' and He specifies the day — that it shall be on the tenth of the seventh month (Leviticus 16:29) — and He returns and says that it shall be once a year (Leviticus 16:34)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Ramban cites the Mekhilta's statement that Nadab and Abihu were מַלִּיזִין אַחֲרֵי הַקְּטֹרֶת, rendered here literally as 'criticizing after the incense.' The word מַלִּיזִין can carry the sense of murmuring or caviling in rabbinic usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:17.717777348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}